{# The Billing Detail / Shipping Detail panel pair a sell-side form carries — the address book
   picker, the frozen snapshot's own editable fields, and the country/province controls that
   re-derive one from the other.

   Shared by templates/admin/order/form.html.twig and templates/admin/estimate/form.html.twig,
   which carried two copies of it: byte-identical once indentation was normalised, 118 lines each,
   with nothing between them but the macro wrapper. Two copies of a document's address panel is how
   one screen quietly gains a field the other never posts — the snapshot is what the customer is
   billed at and shipped to, so a field that goes missing on one form is a document that says
   something different about where the goods went.

   NOT the standalone invoice (admin/invoice/create_standalone.html.twig). Its address panel is
   read-only display text with no picker and no posted fields, and that is a documented rule rather
   than drift: an invoice has no order behind it to inherit a frozen snapshot from, so it copies the
   customer's defaults at save instead of offering them for editing. Nothing here would be right for
   it and it is deliberately left alone.

   Parameters
   ----------
   company          required  the company row (companyToRow()); only `id` is read, for the
                              address-book link
   billingAddress   required  the document's billing snapshot as a row (addressToRow())
   shippingAddress  required  the document's shipping snapshot as a row
   addressBook      required  the customer's saved addresses, as rows, for the picker's <select>

   THE HOOK CLASS NAMES ARE ORDER'S, ON BOTH FORMS, DELIBERATELY. app.js binds
   .js-order-toggle-address-book / .js-order-address-select / .js-order-apply-address /
   .js-order-close-address-book document-wide rather than to the order page specifically, so the
   quote form drives the same picker by reusing the same names — which is exactly why one partial
   can serve both and why these must not be renamed to something document-neutral. Renaming them
   silently breaks the address book on BOTH screens: the markup still renders, the picker just
   stops doing anything. This is the one place the two documents genuinely agree on a name, so it
   is not a parameter.

   The posted field names carry no document prefix either — `billing_address_1`, `shipping_city`
   and the rest — so the two controllers read the panel through the same keys. #}
{% macro address_cards(company, billingAddress, shippingAddress, addressBook) %}
    {% for type, address in {Billing: billingAddress, Shipping: shippingAddress} %}
        {% set typeKey = type|lower %}
        <section class="order-form-panel" data-address-panel="{{ typeKey }}">
            <input type="hidden" name="{{ typeKey }}_address_id" value="{{ address.id|default('') }}" data-address-field="id">
            <h2>
                {{ type }} Detail
                <span class="order-panel-icons">
                    {# A list icon, not a plus: this picks from EXISTING saved addresses, nothing is
                       created here. A plus reads as "add new," which is the one thing this button
                       does not do. #}
                    <button class="order-panel-icon js-order-toggle-address-book" type="button" aria-label="Select {{ type|lower }} address">
                        <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                            <circle cx="4" cy="5" r="1.3"></circle>
                            <rect x="8" y="4" width="9" height="2" rx="1"></rect>
                            <circle cx="4" cy="10" r="1.3"></circle>
                            <rect x="8" y="9" width="9" height="2" rx="1"></rect>
                            <circle cx="4" cy="15" r="1.3"></circle>
                            <rect x="8" y="14" width="9" height="2" rx="1"></rect>
                        </svg>
                    </button>
                    {# An external-link arrow, not four dots: this leaves the panel for the full
                       address book management page — a different screen, not a broader view of
                       the same one. #}
                    <a class="order-panel-icon" href="{{ path('admin_company_address_book', {id: company.id}) }}" aria-label="Go to address page">
                        <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                            <path d="M8 4H4.9C4.4 4 4 4.4 4 4.9v10.2c0 .5.4.9.9.9h10.2c.5 0 .9-.4.9-.9V12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path>
                            <path d="M11 4h5v5M15.6 4.4 9 11" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path>
                        </svg>
                    </a>
                </span>
            </h2>
            <div class="order-address-book js-order-address-book" hidden>
                <h3>Address Book</h3>
                <select class="js-order-address-select" aria-label="{{ type }} address book">
                    <option value=""></option>
                    {% for bookAddress in addressBook %}
                        <option value="{{ bookAddress.id }}"
                            data-company-name="{{ bookAddress.companyName|e('html_attr') }}"
                            data-first-name="{{ bookAddress.firstName|e('html_attr') }}"
                            data-last-name="{{ bookAddress.lastName|e('html_attr') }}"
                            data-phone="{{ bookAddress.phone|e('html_attr') }}"
                            data-address-line1="{{ bookAddress.addressLine1|e('html_attr') }}"
                            data-address-line2="{{ bookAddress.addressLine2|e('html_attr') }}"
                            data-city="{{ bookAddress.city|e('html_attr') }}"
                            data-country="{{ bookAddress.country|e('html_attr') }}"
                            data-province="{{ bookAddress.province|e('html_attr') }}"
                            data-postal-code="{{ bookAddress.postalCode|e('html_attr') }}"
                            data-fax="{{ bookAddress.fax|e('html_attr') }}"
                            data-primary-email="{{ bookAddress.primaryEmail|e('html_attr') }}"
                            data-secondary-email="{{ bookAddress.secondaryEmail|e('html_attr') }}">{{ bookAddress.label }}</option>
                    {% endfor %}
                </select>
                <div class="order-address-actions">
                    <button class="button primary js-order-apply-address" type="button">Apply</button>
                    <button class="button outline js-order-close-address-book" type="button">Close</button>
                </div>
            </div>
            <label class="order-field-row">
                <span>Company name</span>
                <input type="text" name="{{ typeKey }}_company_name" value="{{ address.companyName }}" data-address-field="companyName">
            </label>
            <label class="order-field-row">
                <span>First name</span>
                <input type="text" name="{{ typeKey }}_first_name" value="{{ address.firstName }}" data-address-field="firstName">
            </label>
            <label class="order-field-row">
                <span>Last name</span>
                <input type="text" name="{{ typeKey }}_last_name" value="{{ address.lastName }}" data-address-field="lastName">
            </label>
            <label class="order-field-row">
                <span>Phone number</span>
                <input type="text" name="{{ typeKey }}_phone" value="{{ address.phone }}" data-address-field="phone">
            </label>
            <label class="order-field-row">
                <span>Address line 1</span>
                <input type="text" name="{{ typeKey }}_address_1" value="{{ address.addressLine1 }}" data-address-field="addressLine1">
            </label>
            <label class="order-field-row">
                <span>Address line 2</span>
                <input type="text" name="{{ typeKey }}_address_2" value="{{ address.addressLine2 }}" data-address-field="addressLine2">
            </label>
            <label class="order-field-row">
                <span>City</span>
                <input type="text" name="{{ typeKey }}_city" value="{{ address.city }}" data-address-field="city">
            </label>
            <label class="order-field-row">
                <span>Province</span>
                <select class="js-region-province" name="{{ typeKey }}_province"
                        data-address-field="province"
                        data-province-name="{{ typeKey }}_province"
                        data-selected="{{ address.province|default('') }}">
                    <option value=""></option>
                    {% for code, label in region_provinces(address.country|default('CA') ?: 'CA') %}
                        <option value="{{ code }}" {{ (address.province|default('')) == code ? 'selected' : '' }}>{{ label }}</option>
                    {% endfor %}
                </select>
            </label>
            <label class="order-field-row">
                <span>Country</span>
                <select class="js-region-country" name="{{ typeKey }}_country"
                        data-address-field="country"
                        data-region-map="{{ region_map()|json_encode|e('html_attr') }}"
                        data-province-target="{{ typeKey }}_province">
                    {% set selectedCountry = address.country|default('CA') ?: 'CA' %}
                    {% for code, label in region_countries() %}
                        <option value="{{ code }}" {{ selectedCountry == code ? 'selected' : '' }}>{{ label }}</option>
                    {% endfor %}
                </select>
            </label>
            <label class="order-field-row">
                <span>Postal code</span>
                <input type="text" name="{{ typeKey }}_postal_code" value="{{ address.postalCode }}" data-address-field="postalCode">
            </label>
            <label class="order-field-row">
                <span>Fax</span>
                <input type="text" name="{{ typeKey }}_fax" value="{{ address.fax }}" data-address-field="fax">
            </label>
            <label class="order-field-row">
                <span>Primary email</span>
                <input type="email" name="{{ typeKey }}_primary_email" value="{{ address.primaryEmail }}" data-address-field="primaryEmail">
            </label>
            <label class="order-field-row">
                <span>Secondary email</span>
                <input type="email" name="{{ typeKey }}_secondary_email" value="{{ address.secondaryEmail }}" data-address-field="secondaryEmail">
            </label>
            <label class="order-field-row">
                <span>Delivery instructions</span>
                <textarea name="{{ typeKey }}_delivery_instructions" rows="2"
                          data-address-field="deliveryInstructions"
                          placeholder="Operating days/hours, receiving entrance">{{ address.deliveryInstructions|default('') }}</textarea>
            </label>
        </section>
    {% endfor %}
{% endmacro %}
